69
00:00:26,637 --> 00:00:27,161
generating a force

70
00:00:27,161 --> 00:00:27,510
that counteracted

71
00:00:27,510 --> 00:00:27,860
some of

72
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:28,383
the building's motion.

73
00:00:28,408 --> 00:00:28,760
The dampers

74
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:29,289
absorbed the energy

75
00:00:29,289 --> 00:00:29,818
from these oscillations

76
00:00:29,818 --> 00:00:30,347
and dissipated it

77
00:00:30,347 --> 00:00:30,699
as heat.

78
00:00:30,724 --> 00:00:31,241
As a result,

79
00:00:31,241 --> 00:00:31,586
the building's

80
00:00:31,586 --> 00:00:31,759
movements

81
00:00:31,759 --> 00:00:32,276
became less pronounced.

82
00:00:32,301 --> 00:00:32,672
When another

83
00:00:32,672 --> 00:00:33,230
powerful windstorm hit,

84
00:00:33,230 --> 00:00:33,601
the massive

85
00:00:33,601 --> 00:00:34,159
steel sphere began

86
00:00:34,159 --> 00:00:34,531
swinging back

87
00:00:34,531 --> 00:00:34,902
and forth,

88
00:00:34,902 --> 00:00:35,646
while the people inside

89
00:00:35,646 --> 00:00:36,203
could continue working

90
00:00:36,203 --> 00:00:36,575
more comfortably.

91
00:00:36,599 --> 00:00:37,059
It turns out

92
00:00:37,059 --> 00:00:37,519
that the secret

93
00:00:37,519 --> 00:00:37,826
to keeping

94
00:00:37,826 --> 00:00:38,286
a skyscraper stable

95
00:00:38,286 --> 00:00:38,593
isn't always

96
00:00:38,593 --> 00:00:39,206
making it more rigid...

97
00:00:39,263 --> 00:00:39,631
It's knowing how

98
00:00:39,631 --> 00:00:39,876
to control

99
00:00:39,876 --> 00:00:40,366
the way it moves.
